## The reader does NOT discover Ferrari's vendor reservation

lk2nd/ramoops/ramoops.c:35-53 get_ramoops_region hard-codes:
- size0x80000 (512KiB), record0x2000 (8KiB), console0x40000 (256KiB);
- ftrace/pmsg/ECC zero, leaving dump allocation0x40000 (32 records);
- base = scratch + scratch_size - total_size.

target/msm8916/rules.mk:8-12 gives SCRATCH_ADDR0x90000000;
target/msm8916/meminfo.c:77-85 gives scratch size256MiB.
Calculated defaults, NOT measured runtime placement:
- raw backing [0x9ff80000,0xa0000000);
- dump records [0x9ff80000,0x9ffc0000);
- console allocation [0x9ffc0000,0xa0000000);
- console payload starts0x9ffc000c, maximum0x3fff4 bytes, after the12-byte
  sig/offt/size header (ramoops.c:14-21).
This is SCRATCH-top, not physical RAM-top. It is not vendor0xffe00000/2MiB.

Incoming DT handling (lk2nd/device/2nd/parse-tags.c:28-62 and
lk2nd/device/device.c:107-158) does not set this geometry. The Ferrari entry at
lk2nd/device/dts/msm8916/msm8939-mtp.dts:64-81 has Sharp RSP61322 matching but
no ramoops override; its DTB filename hint remains commented out.

## Outgoing DT hook is opt-in, not retention or byte migration

lk2nd/ramoops/ramoops.c:56-123:
- BOOT_DOWNSTREAM/BOOT_LK2ND returns immediately.
- Otherwise requires lk2nd.pass-ramoops in the hook's command line.
- =zap clears the DEFAULT512KiB before checking for /reserved-memory.
- With an existing /reserved-memory parent, finds/adds compatible ramoops,
  replaces reg and record/console/ftrace/pmsg/ECC sizes with the defaults.
- Without the option, leaves any supplied outgoing node unchanged.
The hook does NOT migrate old bytes from0xffe00000 and adds no FDT memreserve
entry. BOOT_DOWNSTREAM classification includes the /soc/qcom,ion heuristic
(platform/msm_shared/dev_tree.c:2199-2221), not a universal vendor-DT guarantee.
The Android boot path selects a DT from the NEW boot image
(app/aboot/aboot.c:2129-2205); unchanged outgoing DT is not automatic inheritance
of the earlier bootloader's running DT.

